{
  "about": "Shared fixture for sqtk-doorbell.sh's predicate (Story 3.2, R-26; #170). Each case is one SSE event, the squawk ids from the agent's squawk records (numbers, as sqtk-doorbell.sh reads them) and, when known, the squawk's original text (`original`, the script's $bl entry). `rings` is whether sqtk-doorbell.sh's jq rings for it, with the kit's sqtk-answer.jq (vendored beside this file as sqtk-answer.jq). tests/unit/daemon/test_squawkie.py holds the daemon's `rings` and the script's jq, verbatim, to every case.",
  "jq": "include \"sqtk-answer\";\n.type == \"squawk.updated\" and (.squawk.id as $i | $ids[0] | index($i)) != null\nand (.squawk.state != \"open\"\nor (.squawk | sq_answer($bl[0][(.id | tostring)] | strings // null)) != \"\")",
